	(text "Hub carrier for the radio pod (spec 2b): passive. J1 plugs onto hub-core's 2x5 expansion header; J2 is a key board's bay header (same pins, two M2 holes\nplaced by the board script), so the same pod fits. Pod 3.3 V from the Pico's 3.3 V, the pod's 5 V pins from the hub's +5V (level shifter only).\nUART: GP0 (expansion pin 3, UART0 TX of the Pico) -> bay pin 9 (the pod's MISO pin, its input); GP1 (pin 4, UART0 RX) <- bay pin 10 (the pod's MOSI pin,\nits output, 33 R on the pod). hub-core's 4.7 k pull-ups on GP0 / GP1 keep the lines high while idle.\nBay pin 6 (SPARE) is tied to GND: the pod reads it low and knows it sits in the hub. Bay pin 4 (LED data, 5 V level) is open.\nCS -> SP1, SCK -> SP2, INT -> SP3: these reach no Pico pin today (reserved lines of the stack), wired for a later core board; SP4 open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 132.08 0)
